**Definition 6.2 (completed-object registry).** `images` is an append-only
list of $[U(p),b,D]$; lookup scans it completely and retains the last matching
package key. `views` is a list of $[U(q),b,d,D]$, where $q$ is its cardinality
before the new successful publication. $D$ is the actual full sender
descriptor on O/39: measured base, full payload length, owner/port, flags,
and descriptor creation ordinal in RCA's native field order. The adjacent
$b$ field binds that descriptor to its publication; it is not an extra
field silently inserted into the native descriptor grammar. These lists hold
bindings and descriptors, not target snapshots or copies of bodies.

For a successful Call keep its original Image result and package fields.
After its actual publication, print and ACK, import the saved sender
placement record and append $[p,b,D]$ before common return. Repeated calls
of one package can have different sender origins; its last completed
entry is selected and has the same immutable target. The client already
acquired $p$ from Issue; no new image number is tacitly inferred.

For a successful Convert choose $q$ by the actual view-list count, publish
PVC.5 and only after print/ACK append $[q,b,d,D]$. The next service cannot
enter before this bank update, current-frame append, invocation-token TOK
and final Ready. A partial result, setup descriptor or unacknowledged
publication never enters either completed registry.

